{"name":"Blunt","hex":"#b5bbc7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Blunt","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname transferred from the nickname.","A minor city in Hughes County, South Dakota, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Blunt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blunt (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Blunt is a common surname of English derivation, meaning \"blonde, fair\", or \"dull\". A variant spelling is Blount."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blunt_(surname)","wikidata":"Q11215365"},{"title":"Blunt (cigar)","blocks":[{"text":"A blunt is a cigar which is wider than a cigarillo and not quite as wide as a corona, generally equivalent to a petit corona while short panatellas are sometimes classified as mini-blunts. These cigars typically consist of three main parts; an inner, or binder, leaf; an outer wrapper leaf rolled around the binder in a spiral; and chopped tobacco filler. In most commercially available blunts neither the binder nor wrapper is an actual tobacco leaf but made of paper composed of pressed tobacco pulp."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/DunhillEarlyMorningPipeMurrays.jpg/330px-DunhillEarlyMorningPipeMurrays.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blunt_(cigar)","wikidata":"Q886371"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Patch_of_Tobacco_%28Nicotiana_tabacum_%29_in_a_field_in_Intercourse%2C_Pennsylvania..jpg/500px-Patch_of_Tobacco_%28Nicotiana_tabacum_%29_in_a_field_in_Intercourse%2C_Pennsylvania..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Patch_of_Tobacco_%28Nicotiana_tabacum_%29_in_a_field_in_Intercourse%2C_Pennsylvania..jpg/1280px-Patch_of_Tobacco_%28Nicotiana_tabacum_%29_in_a_field_in_Intercourse%2C_Pennsylvania..jpg?utm_source=en.wiki